<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mestwin II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1220–<a href="/years/1294">1294</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Mściwój II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mestwin II (Mściwój II) was the last duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia">Pomerelia</a> from the native Samborides dynasty, ruling the whole of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gdansk">Gdańsk</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> from 1271 to 1294. Lacking sons, he named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/przemysl-ii">Przemysł II</a> of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> his heir in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kepno">Treaty of Kępno</a> of 1282. His death in 1294 opened a contest for the duchy that ended with its seizure by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in 1308.</p></div>
